<h4>Multilingualism</h4>
<p>All translatable fields have the type TaalString. A TaalString is the combination of a textual value with
    an indication of the language. The designation of the language is made on the basis of a
    <a target="_blank" href="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5646.html">language tag</a>. The standard language tags that are supported
    in this deployment model are the following. Please note that new language tags may be supported in due course.    <ul>
        <li>en: Dutch (required)</li>
        <li>English(optional)</li>
        <li>fr: French (optional)</li>
        <li>the: German (optional)</li>
    </ul>
</p>
<p>In the implementation model, the cardinalities for TaalStrings are always indicated from a single language. For example,
    cardinality 1 indicates that exactly 1 textual value is allowed per language. Cardinality 0..1 indicates that there is a
    no or one value is allowed. The exceptional cardinality 0..* indicates that there are several values per language
    are allowed.</p>

<h5>Formal (you) versus informal (you)</h5>
<p>To be able to distinguish between formal texts (u form) and informal texts for Dutch texts
    (your form) some <a target="_blank" href="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5646.html#section-2.2.7">private use language subtags</a> were agreed.    <ul>
        <li>en-BE-x-formal: formal text manually entered by an editor</li>
        <li>en-BE-x-informal: informal text manually entered by an editor</li>
        <li>en-BE-x-generated-formal: automatically generated formal text</li>
        <li>en-BE-x-generated-informal: automatically generated informal text</li>
    </ul>When writing to IPDC or LPDC, or when submitting changes via LDES, only one of the following language tags may be passed: nl-BE-x-formal, nl-BE-x-informal or nl.
    Preferably, nl-BE-x-formal or nl-BE-x-informal. In this way, it is clear in which form the editor wrote the original text.
    When writing to the IPDC or LPDC, the generated tags nl-BE-x-generated-formal and nl-BE-x-generated-informal are not allowed. These will be ignored.    <br/>When reading IPDC, the nl tag will always be present. In addition, either the formal form (nl-BE-x-formal) or generated formal form (nl-BE-x-generated-formal) will always be available.
    As well as the informal form (nl-BE-x-informal) or generated informal form (nl-BE-x-generated-informal) by an editor.</p>

<h5>English</h5>
<p>Organisations with the YourEurope publication channel are made available on the <a target="_blank" href="https://europa.eu/youreurope">YourEurope portal</a>.
    In order to make these instances as findable as possible with a minimum of editing work, these YourEurope instances are automatically translated into English.
    Automatic translated English texts are displayed in the model by the following <a target="_blank" href="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5646.html#section-2.2.7">private use language subtag</a>
    <ul>
        <li>en-x-generated: automatically generated English text</li>
    </ul>
</p>

<h4>Snapshots</h4>
<p>A snapshot shows what an instance or concept looked like at a certain point in time. Every time a functional change is made, a new snapshot will be created
    who captures all attributes and associations filled in at that time. In this way, the complete editorial history of an instance or concept is recorded.
    To keep the diagram clear, the attributes and associations of instances and concepts are not repeated on the snapshot classes.
    In the detailed description of these classes, all attributes and associations can be found.</p>

<h4>Want to know more?</h4>
<p>A complete overview of all available concepts and instances can be found in <a target="_blank" href="https://productencatalogus-v3.vlaanderen.be">the product catalogue</a>.
    Behind the scenes, all these services are stored in <a target="_blank" href="https://www.vlaanderen.be/digitaal-vlaanderen/onze-oplossingen/interbestuurlijke-producten-en-dienstencatalogus-ipdc">IPDC</a>.
    If you wish to integrate the information about this service into your own solutions, this is possible via the
    <a target="_blank" href="https://ipdc.vlaanderen.be/docs/swagger-ui/index.html">IPDC API.</a> Be sure to take a look at
    <a target="_blank" href="https://vlaamseoverheid.atlassian.net/wiki/external/6317081715/ZGU4MGNlODM2N2U1NDU5MGFlY2NlYzcxYmQyYWUwMTc">the connection guide</a>.</p>
